            <ArticleTitle>Transcatheter coil occlusion for treatment of left internal mammary-anterior descending artery steal phenomenon.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>347-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 60-yr-old female with previous bypass surgery including LIMA-LAD graft presented with unstable angina due to steal phenomenon caused by a large pectoral branch of LIMA. Transcatheter coil occlusion of the pectoral branch was successfully performed. This procedure should be considered in similar cases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
